<article class="env-corollary" id="F2CD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F2CD">Corollary <span data-tag="F2CD">2.2.3.13</span>.</a>covariant!equivalence Suppose given a diagram of simplicial sets </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [dr]^{p} \ar [rr]^{f} &  &  Y \ar [dl]^{q} \\ &  S &  } \]
</div>
  <p> where $p$ and $q$ are right fibrations. Then $f$ is a contravariant equivalence in $(\sSet )_{/S}$ if and only if $f$ is a pointwise equivalence. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $(\sSet )_{/S}$ is a simplicial model category, this follows immediately from Corollary <a href="/tag/D778" data-tag="D778">2.2.3.12</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/BB0C" data-tag="BB0C">2.2.3.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>